
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>CSS Background and Link States</title>

    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: lightyellow;
            padding: 20px;
        }

        h1 {
            color: darkblue;
            text-align: center;
        }

        .background-box {
            height: 180px;
            border: 2px solid black;
            padding: 10px;

            background-image:
                url("https://www.transparenttextures.com/patterns/cubes.png");

            background-repeat: repeat;
        }

        a:link {
            color: blue;
        }

        a:visited {
            color: purple;
        }

        a:hover {
            color: red;
            text-decoration: underline;
        }

        a:active {
            color: green;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

    <h1>CSS Background and Link States</h1>

    <h2>Background Repeat Example</h2>

    <div class="background-box">
        This box demonstrates the background-repeat property.
    </div>

    <h2>Different Link States</h2>

    <p><a href="https://www.google.com">Visit Google</a></p>

    <p><a href="https://www.wikipedia.org">Visit Wikipedia</a></p>

    <p>Hover over a link to see its color change.</p>

</body>
</html>
